1
00:03:31,111 --> 00:03:37,111
They were warned...They are doomed...And on Friday
the 13th, nothing will save them.

2
00:07:02,222 --> 00:07:08,222
Friday the 13th is a horror film directed by Sean S. Cunningham.

3
00:10:33,333 --> 00:10:39,333
Camp counselors are stalked and murdered by an unknown assailant while trying to
reopen a summer camp that was the site of a child's drowning.

4
00:14:04,444 --> 00:14:10,444
Alice, played by Adrienne King.

5
00:17:35,555 --> 00:17:41,555
Mrs. Voorhees, played by Betsy Palmer.

6
00:21:06,666 --> 00:21:12,666
Jack, played by Kevin Bacon.

7
00:24:37,777 --> 00:24:43,777
Marcie, played by Jeannine Taylor.

8
00:28:08,888 --> 00:28:14,888
Bill, played by Harry Crosby.

9
00:31:40,000 --> 00:31:46,000
Brenda, played by Laurie Bartram.

10
00:35:11,111 --> 00:35:17,111
Friday the 13th is a 1980 American slasher film produced and directed by Sean S.

11
00:38:42,222 --> 00:38:48,222
Cunningham, written by Victor Miller, and starring Betsy Palmer, Adrienne King, Harry Crosby,
Laurie Bartram, Mark Nelson, Jeannine Taylor, Robbi Morgan, and Kevin Bacon.

12
00:42:13,333 --> 00:42:19,333
The plot follows a group of teenage camp counselors who are murdered one by one by an unknown
killer while they are attempting to reopen an abandoned summer camp with a tragic past.

13
00:45:44,444 --> 00:45:50,444
Prompted by the success of John Carpenter's Halloween (1978), Cunningham put out an advertisement to
sell the film in Variety in early 1979, while Miller was still drafting the screenplay.

14
00:49:15,555 --> 00:49:21,555
After casting the film in New York City, filming took place in New Jersey in the
fall of 1979, on an estimated budget of between $550,000 and $650,000.

15
00:52:46,666 --> 00:52:52,666
A bidding war ensued over the finished film, ending with Paramount Pictures
acquiring the film for domestic distribution, while Warner Bros.

16
00:56:17,777 --> 00:56:23,777
secured international distribution rights.

17
00:59:48,888 --> 00:59:54,888
Friday the 13th became the first independent slasher film to
be acquired by a major motion picture studio.

18
01:03:20,000 --> 01:03:26,000
Released on May 9, 1980, Friday the 13th was a major box office success, grossing $59.8 million worldwide, making it
the fifteenth highest-grossing film of the year, and the second highest-grossing film for Paramount.

19
01:06:51,111 --> 01:06:57,111
The film's critical response was largely unfavorable, with numerous critics deriding it for its
graphic violence, though it did receive some praise for its cinematography and score.

20
01:10:22,222 --> 01:10:28,222
Aside from being the first independent film of its
kind to secure distribution in the U.S.

21
01:13:53,333 --> 01:13:59,333
by a major studio, its box office success led to a long series of sequels, a crossover
with the  A Nightmare on Elm Street film series, and a 2009 series reboot.

22
01:17:24,444 --> 01:17:30,444
A direct sequel, Friday the 13th Part 2, was released one year later.

23
01:20:55,555 --> 01:21:01,555
The film has been subject to critical analysis in film studies for its depiction of youth suffering violent deaths after engaging
in premarital sex, a trope at the center of the film's plot that was frequently used in subsequent slasher films.

24
01:24:26,666 --> 01:24:32,666
It has received mixed retrospective reviews and garnered a cult following.

25
01:27:57,777 --> 01:28:03,777
The film explores themes of lake, new jersey, drowning, summer camp, sadism.

26
01:31:28,888 --> 01:31:34,888
The tone is dark and intense.
